WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.131
R M T I turns what we can measure into one score, and follows it over time.

2
00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:08.950
Here: liver cancer.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.015
Case study: Lau-Min and colleagues, J A M A Network Open, 2025.

4
00:00:13.065 --> 00:00:24.950
Among four thousand one hundred ninety-eight patients on systemic therapy, median survival was eight point one months, and only twenty point seven percent reached second-line treatment.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.950
Stage one. One small tumor, inside the liver, no vessel invasion. Surgery, ablation or transplant can work.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.950
Stage two. The tumor reaches blood vessels, or several small tumors form, still within the liver.

7
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.950
Stage three. Larger or multiple tumors, major vein invasion, and possibly regional lymph nodes.

8
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.950
Stage four. Cells reach distant sites, such as lungs and bones. Treatment turns systemic.

9
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.875
Data assessing.

10
00:00:53.925 --> 00:00:57.144
Liver function, by ALBI grade, informs vulnerability.

11
00:00:57.194 --> 00:00:59.796
Concomitant liver disease informs exposure.

12
00:00:59.846 --> 00:01:05.161
And second-line delivery, reaching only twenty point seven percent, informs resilience.

13
00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:06.950
This mapping is illustrative.

14
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.037
R equals L times E times V times one minus rho.

15
00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:17.559
Here R is zero point zero eight one, band two of the fixed five-band scale.

16
00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:20.950
Expected Annual Loss adds consequences.

17
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:21.782
Trajectory.

18
00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:25.942
Each review cycle updates vulnerability and resilience.

19
00:01:25.992 --> 00:01:36.379
In this synthetic example, as delivery improves, R falls from zero point zero eight one to zero point zero two five, band two to band one.

20
00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.950
An illustration, not a prediction.

21
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.605
What R M T I does.

22
00:01:40.655 --> 00:01:51.180
It quantifies risk as one score, assesses it on fixed bands, and tracks vulnerability and resilience across cycles.

23
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.950
Treatment decisions stay with clinicians.

24
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.019
R M T I is a research prototype: uncalibrated, synthetic examples, not a medical device.

25
00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:04.950
Does trajectory add information beyond the current level?
